# Integer128 comparison ordering

Compares ±10^29 values to verify the equality and ordering relations on
magnitudes far beyond 64 bits. Every operand is int128, keeping this case
focused on same-type relations; mixed widths are covered separately.

>>> source
low: int128 = -100000000000000000000000000000
high: int128 = 100000000000000000000000000000
same: int128 = 100000000000000000000000000000

// Verifies the equality family on equal and distinct operands.
print(high == same)
print(low == high)

// Verifies the ordering family on distinct operands.
print(low < high)
print(high < low)
print(high >= same)
print(low >= high)

<<< stdout
true
false
true
false
true
false

<<< stderr
